 "inferred": {
  "I1": "Revision 5 (E15) makes the entry-to-choice mapping static: first entry 0 = none, second 1 = pick-up, third 2 = value-scaling. Residual: the displayed words of the three text keys are None, Pick-Up, Value Scaling (not read; resources packed). Stated in the contract as an assumption affecting reference labels only.",
  "I2": "The handler registry 0x101b84798/0x10260535c is the MidiMap handler lookup, and dispatch entry +0x30 holds the installed map mode (spec r3 E10 inference).",
  "I3": "The parameter setter 0x101b0d328 (untraced) stores the value without further processing. The contract makes this a precondition and excludes parameters that change a value after it is set.",
  "I4": "Messages are applied in arrival order, once each; the queued-command path taken when 0x1011c0ee8(0x100500) is nonzero has unknown timing. The contract applies messages one at a time and excludes back-to-back ordering, coalescing and deferral.",
  "I5": "Layer wiring from control to component setter, assumed for every target association since spec revision 1.",
  "I6": "arm64 equivalence of the X results: static slice comparison in E16; the only fused operation that differs is the value function fmadd (difference <= 1 binary32 ulp of R, 0 when lo = 0); the takeover fmadd has s1 = +-1.",
  "I7": "The application passes the previous data value as the static dispatcher reading gives it (E10): the last data value on the same input, channel and controller, -129 when none. The X harness supplied it; the dispatcher and the per-input table did not run.",
  "I8": "The harness built the parameter details record (kind, min, max, quantized, Zoom 1.0) and simulated the parameter; which application parameter reports which kind, range and stepping is excluded (PRB-N7-04)."
 },
